// AiAssistChunkCompleted - chora.creation.ai_assist.chunk_completed.v1
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// ADR-251 D5 (CHO-2398): incremental publishing for the set lane's graph chunk
// loop. Emitted by the orchestrator's publish_chunk node when chunk k of a
// multi-chunk job finishes (generate -> critique -> gate -> render), carrying
// that chunk's candidates in PUBLISHED shape: image/render specs stripped,
// per-candidate quality_warning + critic_notes included, exactly the shape the
// terminal AiAssistCompleted.candidate_payload_json entries take. The terminal
// completed.v1 still carries the authoritative FULL set: a consumer that
// ignores chunk events loses nothing but progressiveness (ADR-251 D5, the
// owner-rejected shortcut of riding progress.v1 is recorded in the ADR; one
// event, one meaning - progress.v1 stays trace-only).
//
// Idempotency: envelope.idempotency_key =
// "ai_assist.chunk_completed.{chunk_index}.{assist_id}". Delivery is
// at-least-once and unordered, so the chora-creation consumer persists
// idempotently and MONOTONICALLY by chunk_index per job (a duplicate or
// stale chunk event contributes nothing).
//
// Per ADR-141: envelope.chora_imda_dimension SHOULD = "accountability" (D1).
//
// Topic: chora.creation.ai_assist.chunk_completed.v1
// Consumers: chora-creation ONLY (persist the chunk's candidates into the
//
//	RUNNING ai_assist_jobs row; the question-jobs poll then serves
//	questions-so-far while the job is still running). NOT consumed
//	by governance / observability: the terminal event remains the
//	accountability record.
